.\" Manpage for camio.
.TH CAMIO 1 "2026-11-12" "camio 0.1.0" "Camio Manual"
.SH NAME
camio \- local-first, fingerprint-transparent web security testing workbench
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B camio
.I COMMAND
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Camio
is a Rust web-security testing workbench built around the Camoufox anti-detect
Firefox engine. Tool-originated traffic (Replay, Automate, Scanner, MCP) is sent
through a BoringSSL-based impersonating client whose TLS/JA3/JA4 and HTTP/2
fingerprint is derived from, and pinned to, the same profile the managed browser
uses, so testing traffic does not stand out \fIbecause of the tool\fR.
.PP
Fingerprint transparency means Camio does not add a tool tell on top of the
browser. It is \fBnot\fR a promise of undetectability and does not defeat a
specific target's defenses. Camio is for \fBauthorized testing only\fR.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B engine info|unpack
Show the pinned Camoufox build and download URL, or unpack a downloaded engine.
.TP
.B fingerprint show|spec
Render the anti-detection policy (as \fIuser.js\fR prefs, Camoufox config, or
full profile JSON) or the matched-engine fingerprint spec.
.TP
.B launch
Launch the managed browser with a fingerprint policy applied against an
authorized target URL.
.TP
.B send \fIURL\fR
Send a request through the fingerprint-matched engine. Policy-gated: previews by
default, requires \fB\-\-confirm\fR to send. Supports \fB\-\-rewrite\fR
(Match & Replace).
.TP
.B query \fICAMIOQL\fR
Run a CamioQL (HTTPQL-compatible) query over stored history.
.TP
.B history
Show recent captured exchanges.
.TP
.B scope \fIURL\fR
Report the scope decision for a URL via the one shared scope path (SSRF guard).
.TP
.B convert \fISTEPS\fR
Apply a Convert/Decoder pipeline (base64, url, html, hex, gzip/deflate, hashes).
Use \fB\-\-list\fR to list transforms.
.TP
.B jwt \fITOKEN\fR
Decode a JWT header and payload (signature is NOT verified).
.TP
.B compare \fIA\fR \fIB\fR
Byte/line diff between two files (Comparer).
.TP
.B scan \fR[\fICAMIOQL\fR]
Run passive security checks over stored history; \fB\-\-save\fR persists findings.
.TP
.B fuzz \fIURL\fR
Intruder-class fuzzing over \[char167]...\[char167] insertion points. Shows the
projected request count; sends only with \fB\-\-confirm\fR (active test).
.TP
.B discover \fIURL\fR
Enumerate injectable inputs of a request.
.TP
.B import \fIFILE\fR
Import a Burp items XML export or a HAR archive into history.
.TP
.B sequencer
Estimate token randomness/entropy from samples (one per line).
.TP
.B sitemap \fR[\fICAMIOQL\fR]
Build a site map tree from stored history.
.TP
.B payloads \fR[\fINAME\fR]
List the built-in payload packs, or show one pack's entries.
.TP
.B app
Launch the native desktop workbench (egui). Every capability in one window, with
customizable themes, a plugin system, and an "Open in browser" launcher.
.TP
.B ui
Serve the local web UI on loopback (default 127.0.0.1:8787).
.TP
.B mcp serve
Serve the Model Context Protocol over stdio for an agent/MCP client.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I camio.db
Default SQLite history database in the working directory.
.TP
.I ~/.config/camio/theme.json
Saved native-app theme.
.TP
.I ./plugins/
Directory scanned by the native app for process-based plugins.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Inspect the anti-detection policy:
.PP
.RS
.B camio fingerprint show \-\-preset hardened \-\-format user-js
.RE
.PP
Preview then send a request (authorized target):
.PP
.RS
.B camio send https://example.org \-\-confirm \-H "X-Test: 1"
.RE
.PP
Import a capture, scan it, and view the site map:
.PP
.RS
.B camio import capture.har \-\-db camio.db
.br
.B camio scan \-\-db camio.db \-\-save
.br
.B camio sitemap \-\-db camio.db
.RE
